mmunity Events Alumni Resources Alumni In the News Midland Magazine Midland Legacy Grant Rooted in Faith Campaign About Mission & History Office of the President Midland & Fremont Visitor Guide Board of Directors Faculty & Staff Directory News & Blog Business Partnerships Locations & Maps Careers Heritage Arboretum Title IX & Nondiscrimination Search for: Contact Us Athletics Give WarriorCentral Search Menu Slide CAREER STUDIO Midland University’s Career Studio is your go-to for personalized support — whether you're exploring career paths, polishing your resume, or preparing to land your dream job, we're here to help you every step of the way. SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT Home / Academics / Career Studio In This Section Career Studio Meet the Career Studio Team Career Studio Resources For Students Career Studio Resources for Employers Leadership Midland M-Powered Strengths Midland Mentorship Program Undergraduate Outcomes Report Career & Internship Fair Health & Graduate Fair Midland University Career Studio Midland University’s Career Studio offers a wide range of resources and services to help students prepare for successful careers. From exploring degree and career options to job searching, interviewing, and creating professional resumes or LinkedIn profiles, the Career Studio supports students through every step of the journey. Our dedicated team is committed to helping both students and alumni achieve their career goals. Discover Academic Majors + Career Paths Picking a major is a big part of the college adventure and sets the stage for exciting career possibilities ahead. It’s all about diving into different subjects, discovering unique strengths (hello, CliftonStrengths®), and connecting the dots between what’s studied and what’s next. Explore Majors Prepare for Professional School Programs Learn About CliftonStrengths® Explore Career + Internship Opportunities Jobs and internships are valuable toward building a strong career foundation. From part-time positions to hands-on internships, explore opportunities that offer real-world experience, skill development, and professional connections. Resources for Students Explore Jobs & Internships on Handshake Slide Class of 2025 CAREER OUTCOMES 0% of 2025 grads had a successful career outcomes rate within six months of graduation 6 Months Post-Graduation 80% Response Rate $0 The average starting salary for Midland University's Class of 2025 was $50,000. 0% of graduates completed an internship, practicum, student teaching, or clinical experience. VIEW MORE CAREER OUTCOMES INFO Four Year Career Journey Planning your career doesn’t happen overnight — it’s a journey that unfolds over your four years in college. Each year brings new opportunities to explore your interests, develop your skills, and take actionable steps toward your goals. YEAR ONE: Explore your interests and strengths, build your first resume, attend career events, and start using Handshake. YEAR TWO: Finalize your major, get more involved in campus opportunities, explore internships, update your resume, and create a LinkedIn profile. YEAR THREE: Expand your network, begin searching for internships, attend career events, consider graduate school options, and keep your resume and LinkedIn current. YEAR FOUR: Begin job or grad school applications early, continue updating your materials, attend events, and practice interviewing. Slide CONNECT WITH US The Career Studio team is here to help you explore and prepare for exciting career opportunities ahead. Schedule an appointment, us email at careerstudio@midlandu.edu , check out our socials, or just drop in! SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT EMAIL US Fremont | Omaha | Online Contact Midland University 900 N Clarkson St Fremont, NE 68025 (800) 642-8382 Midland University Omaha 11213 Davenport St #100 Omaha, NE 68154 (402) 941-6226 Resources Careers Media Requests Athletics Arts Faculty & Staff Directory Request a Transcript Marketing & Communications Requests Brand Standards 2026 © Midlan